Additional file 1: Autoactivation of wild-type and E79K trypsinogen at pH 8. Trypsinogen autoactivation was measured in \(100\ \mathrm{mmol/L}\) Tris-HCl pH 8, 1 mmol/L \(\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}\) at \(37^{\circ}\mathsf{C}\) with \(2\ \upmu\mathrm{mol/L}\) trypsinogen and 1 nmol/L or \(10\ \mathrm{nmol/L}\) trypsin at an initial starting concentration. Trypsin activity was determined with CBZ-GPR-pNA as substrate. Additional file 2: Kinetic analysis of PRSS1-WT. Kinetic parameters are given in Table 1. Enzyme was activated by human enteropeptidase (hEPI-Sc-C112S) for 200 min at \(37^{\circ}\mathsf{C}\) in \(100\ \mathrm{mmol/L}\) Tris-HCl pH 8, 1 mmol/L \(\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}\). Assays were performed in \(100\ \mathrm{mmol/L}\) Tris-HCl pH 8, 0, 1 mmol/L \(\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}\) and \(10\ \upmu\mathrm{mol/L}\) to \(1000\ \upmu\mathrm{mol/L}\) CBZ-GPR-pNA at room temperature. The reaction was started by adding PRSS1 variants (12.5 ng) and monitored continuously for 5 min by an absorbance measurement at \(405\ \mathrm{nm}\) (extinction coefficient for p-nitroaniline \(\varepsilon=10092\ \mathrm{L/mol/cm}\)). Additional file 3: Kinetic analysis of PRSS1-sc. Kinetic parameters are given in Table 1. Enzyme was activated by human enteropeptidase (hEPI-Sc-C112S) for \(200\ \mathrm{min}\) at \(37^{\circ}\mathsf{C}\) in \(100\ \mathrm{mmol/L}\) Tris-HCl pH 8, 0, 1 mmol/L \(\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}\). Assays were performed in \(100\ \upmu\mathrm{mol/L}\) CBZ-GPR-pNA at room temperature. The reaction was started by adding PRSS1 variants (12.5 ng) and monitored continuously for 5 min by an absorbance measurement at \(405\ \mathrm{nm}\) (extinction coefficient for p-nitroaniline \(\varepsilon=10092\ \mathrm{L/mol/cm}\)).
